title: Terms & Conditions – The Vocabulary of the Faith
description: A working glossary of the words we build our doctrine on: salvation, the Godhead, God's sovereign plan, the Christian life, the end times and rightly dividing the Word.
output: lessons/doctrine/doctrine-week-6-terms-and-conditions.html

# Doctrine Week 6. The old page's tap-a-word glossary cards become panels with verse buttons; its pictures
# are saved next to the deck as doctrine-week-6-terms-and-conditions-<n>.jpg in their old order.

=== Introduction
--- Terms & Conditions [title]
overline: Faith Baptist Church of Plymouth County · Adult Sunday School · Week 6
heading: Terms & Conditions
sub: The vocabulary of the faith: plain definitions for the words we build our doctrine on
p: Every field of study has its own language, and theology is no exception. Before we can rightly divide the Word, we need to agree on what its key terms actually mean. Tap any gold reference for its supporting Scripture.
note: A Working Glossary

=== I. How We Are Saved
--- How We Are Saved: Grace, Faith, Repentance
lead: **Soteriology**: the doctrines and teachings of salvation. Six terms that describe how a sinner comes to stand right before a holy God.
panel: Grace | The unmerited, unearned, undeserved favor of God. Mercy extended to someone by the unconditional love of another. The favorable influence of God on persons and situations. [[Romans 11:6]]
panel: Faith | The persuasion of mind that something is true, trustworthy, and able to be counted on, without having seen direct evidence. Belief and trust in someone’s word are the characteristics of faith. Every man is given a measure of faith by God ([[Romans 12:3]]). [[Hebrews 11:1]] [[Ephesians 1:12-14]]
panel: Repentance | A change of mind or heart when presented with new information. The Greek *metanoeo* means “to change one’s mind.” The emphasis is on a shift in thinking and perspective, not on feeling remorse or regret. Sorrow at wrongdoing being pointed out can lead to repentance, but is not repentance itself. [[Jonah 3:10]] [[Acts 19:5]] [[2 Corinthians 7:10]]

--- How We Are Saved: Salvation, Justification, Propitiation
panel: Salvation | The deliverance from sin and its consequences, by grace through faith in Jesus Christ. It is a gift of God, not something earned by works, a one-time event that, once secured, cannot be lost. “Save,” “saved,” and “salvation” are also used in Scripture for physical rescue, depending on context. [[Ephesians 2:8-9]] [[John 10:28-29]] [[Jude 5]]
panel: Justification | The act of God by which He declares a sinner to be righteous and free from the guilt of sin. This is a legal declaration based on the righteousness of Christ imputed to the believer through faith: “just as I’ve never sinned.” [[Romans 5:1]] [[Romans 4:5]]
panel: Propitiation | The act of appeasing or satisfying God’s holy wrath against sin. Jesus Christ, through His death on the cross, is the propitiation for our sins. [[1 John 2:2]]

--- Hebrews 11:1
image: lessons/doctrine/doctrine-week-6-terms-and-conditions-1.jpg | Now faith is the substance of things hoped for, the evidence of things not seen. Hebrews 11:1 | [[Hebrews 11:1]]

