image: lessons/doctrine/doctrine-week-6-terms-and-conditions-3.jpg | Biblical Repentance: repent means to change your mind, from unbelief to belief | Biblical Repentance

--- Past, Present & Future
lead: Justification, sanctification, and glorification are three tenses of the same salvation: a past event, a present process, and a future certainty.
image: lessons/doctrine/doctrine-week-6-terms-and-conditions-4.jpg | Three tenses of salvation: past justification, present sanctification, future glorification | Past, Present & Future: Justification, Sanctification, Glorification

--- Every Belief System Reduces to One of Two Doors
image: lessons/doctrine/doctrine-week-6-terms-and-conditions-5.jpg | There are only 2 religions in this world: Faith in Christ, or Faith in works | Every Belief System Reduces to One of Two Doors

=== II. The Godhead
--- The Godhead: Trinity, Godhead, Holy
lead: Who God is: His triune nature, and the attributes that belong to Him alone.
panel: Trinity | The theological name for the concept of the Godhead: the three persons of God: the Father, the Son, and the Holy Spirit. [[1 John 5:7]]
panel: Godhead | The essential being, or nature, of God. All persons of the Trinity are of the Godhead. [[Colossians 2:9]]
panel: Holy | Hallowed; consecrated or set apart to a sacred use, or to the service or worship of God, as with the holy sabbath, holy oil, holy vessels, a holy nation, the holy temple, a holy priesthood. God Himself is holy, being perfect and separated from all things that aren’t holy.

--- The Godhead: Omnipotent, Omniscient
panel: Omnipotent | All-powerful. A trait found only in the Godhead. [[Revelation 19:6]]
panel: Omniscient | All-knowing. A trait found only in the Godhead. [[1 John 3:20]]

--- The Shield of the Trinity
image: lessons/doctrine/doctrine-week-6-terms-and-conditions-6.jpg | The Father Is God, The Son Is God, The Holy Spirit Is God, but the Father is not the Son, the Son is not the Spirit, the Spirit is not the Father | The Shield of the Trinity

=== III. God’s Sovereign Plan
--- God’s Sovereign Plan
lead: How God’s choosing and man’s believing work together in salvation.
panel: Elect | Chosen. The saved: the sons and daughters of God. God determined that all who believe on Christ Jesus would be the elect.
panel: Predestination | The act of God determining something to be so before it occurs. Jesus was predestined to be the Lamb slain to take away the sins of the world. In terms of salvation, God predestined the means and results of salvation, not who specifically would be saved. [[Revelation 13:8]] [[Romans 8:29-31]] [[Ephesians 1:4-11]]
panel: Reprobate | Rejected. In the context of salvation, it refers to those given over to a reprobate mind because they rejected the truth of God and held it in unrighteousness: conscience seared as with a hot iron, filled with all unrighteousness, unable to come to the knowledge of the truth. [[Romans 1:28]]

=== IV. The Christian Life
--- The Christian Life: Sanctification and Separation
lead: Salvation is a gift, received once. What follows, a lifetime of being set apart and following Christ, is a different matter altogether.
panel: Sanctification | The process by which a believer is set apart from sin and made holy: both a lifelong process that begins at salvation and continues until the Rapture, AND the finished work of the Spirit on our spirit, made clean by the blood of Christ. Our sanctification will never be perfect; the sanctification of the Spirit is perfect. [[1 Thessalonians 4:3]] [[1 Thessalonians 5:23]]
panel: Separation | A biblical doctrine commanding believers to be separate from sin, the world, and false doctrine: personal separation in conduct and character, as well as separation from churches and organizations that do not hold to sound doctrine, and from people who compel us toward sin. We are separated not only from the world, but toward the doctrines of God. [[2 Corinthians 6:17]] [[1 Peter 2:11-12]]

--- The Christian Life: Disciple and Apostle
panel: Disciple | A follower of someone or something. In Christianity, it is following Christ not just as a saved believer, but walking in Him, in the Spirit, and denying yourself to serve others. It is not a requirement for salvation, but a calling we all have. Not all believers are disciples. We must choose to pick up our cross and follow Him, and being a disciple has a cost. [[Matthew 16:24]] [[Luke 14:28-30]]
panel: Apostle | Literally, a person sent by another; a messenger, an envoy. A special follower of Christ, used as a witness to His life and to spread the Gospel, generally applied to the twelve chosen for this purpose. [[Mark 3:14]]

